# 7. HOW TO BUILD THE FIRST DATA TEAM

Research what an organization should consider when creating its first formal data team.

Investigate:

- business strategy
- organizational readiness
- executive sponsorship
- mission
- scope
- initial use cases
- team charter
- organizational reporting line
- initial roles
- hiring
- internal talent
- technical infrastructure
- data availability
- governance
- security
- privacy
- stakeholder management
- prioritization
- early wins
- measurement

Answer:

> **What should an organization do during its first 3, 6, and 12 months?**

Only make recommendations supported by evidence or clearly label them as synthesis.

